## Context
The overwrite negative control added in ticket 0238 (PR #287) clobbers
.git/description to prove the snapshot detects in-place content changes.
That file exists only because git's default template ships it: under a
stripped or custom init.templateDir the control would silently degrade to
a vacuous creation test. Non-blocking /verify minor on PR #287; works on
standard git init everywhere CI runs today, so low urgency -- hermeticity
polish, not a live bug.

## Relevant files
- `tests/test_scopeconfinement.sh` -- overwrite negative control block (clobbers $repo/.git/description)

## Actions
1. In the overwrite control, create the control's own file outside
   tickets/ in the scratch repo (e.g. probe.txt at repo root), snapshot,
   overwrite its content (same byte length, to also prove the signature
   is content-based not size-based), snapshot, assert difference.
2. Drop the .git/description dependency.

## Test
Red step: temporarily simulate a stripped template (delete .git/description
in the scratch repo before the control runs) and confirm the CURRENT
control passes vacuously; then switch to the self-created file and confirm
detection still trips.

## Invariants
- Suite stays hermetic and POSIX-shell only.
- All 18 confined commands and both existing controls keep passing (20/20 baseline from 0238).

## Exit criteria
- [x] Overwrite control creates and overwrites its own file (no git template dependency)
- [x] Same-length overwrite is detected (content-based proof)
- [x] make check passes
